The canonical tests resolve the examples as documentation mistakes: the required outputs are ordered by `(popcount(abs(x)), x)`, e.g. `[1,5,2,3,4] → [1,2,4,3,5]`. The frozen semantics directly models `bin`, string `count`, stable numeric `sorted`, and an intentionally opaque keyed-sort primitive. I’ll implement a two-pass stable sort so tie-breaking remains expressible in the supported subset.
